        "additionalInstructions": "The run input names the issue and the base branch. Before planning, check that the issue is not already handled: run `gh pr list --state all --limit 200 --json number,state,url,body --jq '[.[] | select(.state != \"CLOSED\") | select(.body | test(\"(?i)(close[sd]?|fix(e[sd])?|resolve[sd]?)[[:space:]]+#<issue>([^0-9]|$)\")) | {number,state,url}]'` with <issue> replaced by the issue number. If it lists any PR (open or merged), stop: do not plan, and report failure with a summary naming each PR (number, state, url). PRs into non-default branches do not auto-close issues, so a merged PR can exist while the issue is still open. Otherwise report the plan in data.plan, and also echo data.issue (number) and data.baseBranch so later nodes can read them.",
