  "description": "Implements one GitHub issue end to end: plan (Opus) → codegen → implement (Hydrogen medium, ponytail, once) → review (Sonnet, code-review + ponytail-review) → quality gate → PR → wait for CI, with an investigate/fix loop on CI failure. A review rejection or a gate failure goes to implement_fix (Neon medium), at most twice each, then back to review. Review runs before the gate so a rejected change does not pay for a full gate run. The gate finds its base branch itself (the closest of origin/development and origin/spec/*). The plan node first stops the run if an open or merged PR already closes the issue. Run input: \"Implement issue #<n>. Base branch: <branch>.\" (the Spec Implementation fan-out sends this per ticket, with base spec/<n>). Never merges: the PR is left for the parent workflow or a human. Start it in a new worktree.",
  "entryNodeId": "plan",
  "schemaVersion": 1
}
